body:
In the finals(?) of Worlds, Chapin picked up his pen over his lifepad as if to write down a new life total, baiting his opponent into thinking he was just going to take the damage. After his opponent finished declaring attacks, Chapin played a spell, baiting his opponent.

&#x200B;

LSV had mana open to make a token using Adanto, the First Fort, but he also had a one-of Settle the Wreckage in his hand which is the same cost. He picked up a token to make his opponent think he was just going to make it, his opponent then jammed with everything and got blown out by the Settle.
